# Wasp Drops Its Custom Language — TypeScript SDK ...
created: 2026-05-27, last updated: 2026-06-23, [Read more](https://byteiota.com/wasp-drops-custom-language-typescript-sdk/)

After five years and $5M, the team behind the full-stack React + Node.js + Prisma framework is replacing its bespoke `.wasp` DSL with a TypeScript SDK.
...
The surface change is a file rename and a new import.
Your `main.wasp` becomes `main.wasp.ts`.
The new API uses a constructor from the `wasp-config` package:
```
// Old DSL (main.wasp)
app myApp {
wasp: { version: "^0.23.0" },
title: "My App",
...
}
...
page HomePage {
...
```
// New TypeScript SDK (main.wasp.ts)
import { App } from 'wasp-config'
const app = new App('myApp', {
title: 'My App',
wasp: { version: '^0.23' }
})
app.auth({
userEntity: 'User',
methods: { google: {} }
})
app.route('HomeRoute', { path: '/', to: 'HomePage' })
app.page('HomePage', {
component: { import: 'Home', from: '@src/pages/Home' }
})
export default app
```

